From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:14:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Enforce dedup in the database and version the cron
 schedule

Dedup: the scraper pre-read 30 days of source_urls into a Set, with no explicit
limit, so PostgREST capped it at 1000 rows. Past 1000 articles in the window the
Set was silently incomplete and duplicates accumulated - nothing prevented them,
source_url carried only a hash index. Collapse existing duplicates keeping the
earliest row, add UNIQUE (source_url), and let the scraper upsert.

Schedule: grep found no cron.schedule or http_post anywhere in the migrations.
The repository activated pg_cron and pg_net but scheduled nothing, so any
refresh that ran was created by hand in the SQL editor - unreviewable and not
reproducible. The daily sweep is now defined in code, reading its credentials
from Vault and degrading to a NOTICE when the secrets are absent rather than
failing the migration.

